We have an RA8000 with 24 drives split into 4 arrays horizontally.
Total capacity is around 800GB. Each array is configured as raid5
and then I created an ADVFS domain composed of each of those arrays
(4 devices if you will).

The system is pretty much flawless with regard to this accept for
one aspect. We move a LOT of data on, off and around this raid. Lot
meaning approximately a minimum of 100GB a day. Some days it might be
40 other days it might be 200.  The problem is fragmentation.

From what I have gathered on stats usually we do not see a major
impact on performace until around 40% as reported by defragment -nv.
Unfortunately I can defrag this system over the weekend and by time
8am Monday rolls around its already down to about 70%. I also balance
the advfs domain. By Tuesday morning its nothing to see the
aggregate IO down to like 30-35%. This is having a severe issue with
performance.

Does anyone have a suggestion to get around this?  We have put
together a lower end raid for simple storage and it has alleviated
the primary issue but it has anything but solved it.

Is there perhaps something I can do to help prevent this
fragmentation via tweaking or is this just a fact of dealing with
advfs and the movement of this amount of data?

TIA.


