was a little preplexed on which box I should get. I finally decided to 
take my chances on an ebay box advertised as a '500a with the onboard 
scsi.' turns out, the thing is badged as a 500a but reports as a 500au 
(upgraded?). two issues made themselves apparent: the machine came with 
only 128MB memory and a matrox video card. newsgroup digging showed i 
may be able to get away with better-than-pc66 sdrams in the slots if i 
at least matched the rest of the machine's requirements or expectations 
(CL2, ECC, unbuffered.. according to crucial). crucial's only 'official' 
option was a 128MB sdram.. costly at $50/ea if I want .5G. So I matched 
as close as possible to the 256MB SDRAMS (p/n CT32M72S4D7E).. and damn 
if the things don't work! what suprised me more is I put the original 
Dec chips in as a test, thinking the timing difference would piss the 
box off.. and it didn't! so i have 640MB in the little stinker.

problem 2 (the video card) will be solved shortly thanks to this 
excellent page[0] out in the net. Hard to find these cards at this e 
point.. but not impossible. And i don't really need graphics anyway; I 
can use serial or SSH and be satisfied. windows would be nice now and then..

just wanted to toss a datapoint out there for anyone who might want to 
boost the memory in their box and not shell out major bucks for it. I 
did it for $120 ($60/ea) instead of the 4x$50 I was looking at. I just 
wanted to share..

