"sam" <samwun@hgcbroadband.com> wrote in message
news:beh3s1$2m75$1@news.hgc.com.hk...
> Hi,
>
> I would like to change encryption method of the password in 4.0F.
> The problem now is I don't know which file I should edit to change the
> encryption method and I want to use Blowfish but not sure whether 4.0F
> support Blowfish encyrption.
>
> Thanks
> sam
>

V4.0F uses crypt(3) to encrypt users passwords if you are
using Base security.  If you have enabled Enhanced Security
you can select crypt or bigcrypt (similar to crypt, but allows
longer passwords).

The only way to change the encryption method to something
else in V4.0F would be to write your own SIA mechanism
to do so.  Writing your own SIA mechanism to do this would
most likely be possible, but very complicated and time
consuming.  There is information on writing an SIA mechanism
in the Security manual Programming section.

The functionality to allow you to easily add other encryption
methods for users passwords was added in a later version
(v5.0 I think).

Ann




