Wouldn't worry about it we see them all the time. My understanding is
that a NFS connection between the client and server has been broken
without one of the parties being ideally notified. Therefore it still
has a NFS stale link - but is has probably resestablished a new link
in meantime. My guessing it is the the client?

I wouldn't mind a technical description of what this actually means.
All I know is it is nothing to worry about as long as you can still
connect between your clients and the server.


